        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "L3  LQM2MPN1R0NGHL (EthernetAndPower sheet, series element between IC2 SW and the +3V3 output node)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The board is built with a different inductor than the specified/recommended part; its tolerance (and possibly saturation-current rating) differ, so the 3.3 V/1 A buck's ripple current, efficiency and full-load saturation margin will deviate from the intended design. It can saturate/trip earlier than intended at high load.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing implements the Meshinger design essentially as specified (SKW92A module, FAN53610 buck with EN=VIN and FB=+3V3, PDI-matched EPD driver, barrel-jack battery disconnect, slide switch on HW_RESET), but the buck converter's output inductor is a different Murata part (LQM2MPN1R0NGHL) than the LQM2MPN1R0MGHL required by the specification/datasheet recommendation - a sourcing/part-selection deviation."
}

